 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
--   **Axial Resolution:** Volumes with low axial resolution (e.g., CT6, MRI3) have less inter-slice correlation. The performance gain of advanced kernels (9x7, 6,6) over integer kernels may be reduced along the axial dimension [S1].
--   **Precision:** 5x3 uses rational coefficients with powers-of-two dividends to ensure perfect reversibility. Using floating-point approximations for 5x3 can introduce rounding errors that break lossless reconstruction [S1].
--   **Complexity:** (6,6) and 9x7 have higher computational complexity than Haar and 5x3 due to more lifting steps and longer support [S1].
