 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** Higher for 9x7 and (6,6) due to more lifting steps and longer filter support compared to Haar and 5x3 [S1].
--   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the number of coefficients stored. 5x3 and Haar are integer-based, potentially allowing more compact storage if quantization is applied, but 5x3 is preferred for lossless [S1].
--   **Performance:**
-    -   **Lossless:** 5x3 > Haar [S1].
-    -   **Lossy/Near-Lossless:** (6,6) $\approx$ 9x7 > 5x3 > Haar. (6,6) outperforms 9x7 for 7/11 images [S1]. BD-PSNR improvements up to 2 dB for 9x7/(6,6) vs 5x3 at 0.5–3.0 bpp [S1].
--   **Strengths:** 5x3 offers perfect reversibility. 9x7/(6,6) offer superior energy compaction for lossy coding.
--   **Limitations:** 9x7/(6,6) are irreversible. Haar is inefficient for lossless compared to 5x3.
